  "title": "FCM clearing concentration and high-volatility crowding-out of small commodity traders",
  "seed": 1694,
  "run_utc": "2026-07-28T23:00:56.030577+00:00",
  "verdict": "NULL",
  "verdict_scope": "NULL means the negative, binary high-vol crowding-out hypothesis (spec1 fcm_x_highvol < 0) is NOT SUPPORTED. 'Not supported' is the whole claim: these estimators cannot establish that the effect is absent, and NULL does NOT mean 'no association'. The continuous analogue (spec2 fcm_x_rvz) is POSITIVE and significant: coef 2.8750e-04, t_DK 2.54, t_cluster_month 2.56 -- i.e. in the direction opposite to crowding-out.",
  "claim_type": "ex_post_association",
  "claim_language_rule": "NO specification here supports a predictive, causal, forecast or known-before-outcome claim, and none supports 'there is no predictability'. spec1-3 are ex-post association because the FCM report can become available mid-outcome-month while the outcome is a whole-month average change. spec4 hardens the timing (month-start as-of merge, point-in-time regime label at t-1, t-2 DCOT controls, its own sample) but its ex-ante status is CONDITIONAL on the synthetic availability constant, so its null is 'no association survives this timing', not 'no predictability'. Null results are stated as NOT SUPPORTED, never as disproved.",
